1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:01,388
[sighs]

2
00:00:02,806 --> 00:00:03,640
[groans]

3
00:00:04,808 --> 00:00:06,226
[moans]

4
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:09,521
Yah-hoo!

5
00:00:09,604 --> 00:00:12,024
-Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!
-[Tsukasa] Hey.

6
00:00:12,107 --> 00:00:13,525
-Woo-hoo. Woo-hoo.
-[Junta] Um…

7
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:14,901
Your friend?

8
00:00:15,527 --> 00:00:16,862
Great question.

9
00:00:16,945 --> 00:00:19,865
The name's Junta Hayami,
we're childhood friends.

10
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:22,951
Did-- Did you sleep here?

11
00:00:23,035 --> 00:00:26,496
This is my friend, Kazuki. Funny story,
he has a string of back luck,

12
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,957
so he's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

13
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,960
He's… crashing here?

14
00:00:32,044 --> 00:00:34,296
Yeah, it's a really long story.

15
00:00:34,379 --> 00:00:36,298
-I'm just gonna go.
-[Riri giggling, cheering]

16
00:00:36,381 --> 00:00:37,215
Yeah. Sure.

17
00:00:37,716 --> 00:00:39,634
[groans]
I forgot my bag.

18
00:00:42,053 --> 00:00:43,013
Hmm.

19
00:00:44,765 --> 00:00:45,974
[sighs]

20
00:00:48,101 --> 00:00:49,061
[Tsukasa] He's tall.

21
00:00:49,561 --> 00:00:51,146
[Junta] He's really good-looking.

22
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,862
[theme music]

23
00:02:22,112 --> 00:02:23,113
-[grunts, roars]
-[yells]

24
00:02:23,196 --> 00:02:25,949
#4 THE CHILDHOOD FRIEND IS EASY MODE

25
00:02:26,032 --> 00:02:27,075
A victory!

26
00:02:28,201 --> 00:02:29,035
[grunts]

27
00:02:29,119 --> 00:02:31,454
[groans, yells]

28
00:02:33,665 --> 00:02:36,459
-Hey! Explain yourself, you devil!
-[Riri] Wait! I'm Riri!

29
00:02:36,543 --> 00:02:39,087
Your helpful wizard friend, not the devil!

30
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,715
You're no friend of mine.

31
00:02:41,798 --> 00:02:45,969
And what's with that guy out there?
He keeps saying we're childhood friends.

32
00:02:46,052 --> 00:02:48,471
Reuniting with a childhood friend.

33
00:02:48,555 --> 00:02:50,974
Another classic romance scenario.

34
00:02:51,057 --> 00:02:52,434
ROMANTIC THRILLER

35
00:02:52,517 --> 00:02:55,896
[Riri] The two of you grew up together.
You were inseparable.

36
00:02:55,979 --> 00:03:00,984
Before you know it, those feelings
of friendship turned into sparks of love.

37
00:03:01,067 --> 00:03:02,485
-…the problem here.
-Let me take a look at it.

38
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:07,240
What? I don't remember having a friend
like that, especially one that's so cute.

39
00:03:07,824 --> 00:03:10,160
Well, his name is Junta Hayami.

40
00:03:10,243 --> 00:03:12,954
And you've been besties
since elementary school.

41
00:03:13,038 --> 00:03:14,748
But it's a lie. It's not true!

42
00:03:15,749 --> 00:03:19,127
Junta's the hottest rookie
on the school's baseball team this year.

43
00:03:19,210 --> 00:03:21,254
After being separated
for three long years,

44
00:03:21,338 --> 00:03:23,006
you've been reunited.

45
00:03:23,089 --> 00:03:25,008
[Anzu] That's an oddly specific backstory.

46
00:03:25,091 --> 00:03:27,260
I haven't even told you the best part yet.

47
00:03:27,844 --> 00:03:32,015
Junta's had a secret crush on you
since elementary school!

48
00:03:32,098 --> 00:03:33,516
Don't do this to him!

49
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:38,271
[Riri] Do you get it? All you have to do
to win the game is accept his feelings.

50
00:03:38,355 --> 00:03:42,359
I call it Easy Mode in Romantic Thriller.

51
00:03:42,442 --> 00:03:44,277
You call this "Easy Mode"!

52
00:03:44,361 --> 00:03:46,363
Just go away, devil.

53
00:03:46,863 --> 00:03:48,406
Now, begone, evil spirit!

54
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:51,284
I've already told you
I'm not the devil or an evil spirit.

55
00:03:52,244 --> 00:03:54,704
How did I end up
in such a ridiculous spot?

56
00:03:54,788 --> 00:03:57,874
When you think about it,
it's not all that ridiculous.

57
00:03:57,958 --> 00:04:01,628
Having a crush on your best friend
is a classic scenario.

58
00:04:01,711 --> 00:04:04,089
Hey, stop putting
these dumb thoughts into my head.

59
00:04:04,172 --> 00:04:05,799
You're cute when you're embarrassed.

60
00:04:05,882 --> 00:04:07,509
-Who you're calling cute?
-[groans]

61
00:04:07,592 --> 00:04:09,511
[footsteps]

62
00:04:09,594 --> 00:04:12,597
[Anzu] Crap, what was his name? Jun… Jo…

63
00:04:12,681 --> 00:04:14,015
-[Riri] You mean Junta?
-[door closes]

64
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:18,019
Yeah, he's been out there
for a while now, hasn't he?

65
00:04:18,103 --> 00:04:21,022
Oh, don't worry. I took care of that.

66
00:04:21,106 --> 00:04:26,027
He's in his own scenario, see? He's been
chatting with you this whole time.

67
00:04:26,861 --> 00:04:28,530
-Kirarin!
-[Junta] Uh, sorry.

68
00:04:29,114 --> 00:04:32,033
I'm not all that familiar
with torture methods.

69
00:04:32,117 --> 00:04:34,411
[Anzu] What the hell
were we talking about?

70
00:04:36,997 --> 00:04:40,375
I got to say I was surprised earlier.

71
00:04:41,042 --> 00:04:44,045
I swear I don't usually
talk about torture.

72
00:04:44,129 --> 00:04:45,588
It wasn't about that.

73
00:04:47,173 --> 00:04:48,758
It was Kazuki.

74
00:04:49,426 --> 00:04:51,219
[Anzu] Kazuki? What about him?

75
00:04:51,303 --> 00:04:53,305
Look, I think it's great
that you're helping a friend

76
00:04:53,388 --> 00:04:55,098
out of a bad situation,

77
00:04:55,181 --> 00:04:57,350
but it's rude of him
to put you out like that.

78
00:04:57,934 --> 00:05:01,980
Put me out? Nah, doesn't bother me.
The room was empty, anyway.

79
00:05:02,772 --> 00:05:05,734
Right, but… you sure it's a good idea?

80
00:05:05,817 --> 00:05:07,861
I mean, how well do you really know him?

81
00:05:07,944 --> 00:05:11,489
[Anzu] Seriously, I know a lot more
about him than I do about you.

82
00:05:12,198 --> 00:05:16,619
No worries. Kazuki's not great
at first impressions, but he's a good guy.

83
00:05:16,703 --> 00:05:20,498
Besides, he's got so many fangirls,
he's totally over the whole scene.

84
00:05:21,583 --> 00:05:23,668
[Junta] I see, well, okay.

85
00:05:23,752 --> 00:05:26,254
I guess if your parents were cool
with him staying at your place,

86
00:05:26,338 --> 00:05:28,631
then I shouldn't be
too worried about it, either.

87
00:05:29,215 --> 00:05:31,342
[Anzu] Maybe you should try
worrying less about him

88
00:05:31,426 --> 00:05:33,219
and worrying more
about yourself there, buddy.

89
00:05:33,303 --> 00:05:34,637
MIND CONTROL BY THE DEVIL

90
00:05:34,721 --> 00:05:37,432
[sighs]
This whole thing is my fault.

91
00:05:37,515 --> 00:05:38,349
What?

92
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:40,143
Uh, nothing, really.

93
00:05:40,226 --> 00:05:42,145
[wind whooshing]

94
00:05:42,729 --> 00:05:45,023
-[grunts]
-Hey, what's going on in here?

95
00:05:45,106 --> 00:05:46,900
-This wind is so strong.
-Are you okay?

96
00:05:46,983 --> 00:05:48,234
[grunts]

97
00:05:48,318 --> 00:05:49,277
[Anzu] Yeah.

98
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:50,570
-[Junta] Anzu.
-[Anzu] Huh?

99
00:05:51,237 --> 00:05:53,740
[dreamy music]

100
00:05:53,823 --> 00:05:55,158
-[heart thumping]
-H-- Hey…

101
00:05:56,534 --> 00:05:57,660
Just hold still.

102
00:05:57,744 --> 00:06:00,038
-[thumping continues]
-[weak moan]

103
00:06:00,121 --> 00:06:01,164
[Junta] You've got…

104
00:06:01,247 --> 00:06:03,666
a Hercules beetle stuck in your hair.

105
00:06:04,751 --> 00:06:05,668
What?

106
00:06:05,752 --> 00:06:07,754
[screams]
What the…

107
00:06:07,837 --> 00:06:10,256
What is that thing? It's freaking huge!

108
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:12,342
-[Junta] Quit squirming.
-[Anzu] Ah, no, no, no, no. Ah!

109
00:06:12,425 --> 00:06:15,678
-[Junta] Oh, it's really tangled in there.
-[Anzu] Hurry up! Get it off me!

110
00:06:15,762 --> 00:06:16,805
[Junta grunts]

111
00:06:18,264 --> 00:06:19,182
Ta-da!

112
00:06:19,265 --> 00:06:21,184
SINCE IT IS UNSIGHTLY,
WE'VE CONVERTED IT TO A CREPE.

113
00:06:22,143 --> 00:06:23,686
Oh, gross! Get it away from me!

114
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:25,814
-Get rid of that thing!
-Uh, uh…

115
00:06:25,897 --> 00:06:26,898
My bad. Sorry.

116
00:06:28,233 --> 00:06:30,026
[exclaims]
Look how big this one is.

117
00:06:30,110 --> 00:06:32,278
I'll bet you it's worth
at least a hundred dollars.

118
00:06:32,362 --> 00:06:36,533
One hundred?
That ugly beetle's worth that much?

119
00:06:36,616 --> 00:06:38,201
[buzzing]

120
00:06:40,411 --> 00:06:41,830
Stop it!

121
00:06:41,913 --> 00:06:42,914
Catch it!

122
00:06:43,414 --> 00:06:45,333
-I think I can still reach it.
-[pants]

123
00:06:45,416 --> 00:06:46,334
Incoming!

124
00:06:47,001 --> 00:06:47,836
It's gonna hurt.

125
00:06:47,919 --> 00:06:49,337
[yells]

126
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,339
[gasps]
Anzu!

127
00:06:56,302 --> 00:06:57,595
[buzzing]

128
00:06:58,805 --> 00:07:00,682
I… got you.

129
00:07:01,683 --> 00:07:02,725
[pants]

130
00:07:03,518 --> 00:07:06,604
Um, nice catch. Great reflexes.

131
00:07:07,355 --> 00:07:10,066
Oh, thanks. Just glad you're okay.

132
00:07:11,818 --> 00:07:14,154
[Anzu] Ugh, damn it, Junta.
Why do you have to be such a great guy?

133
00:07:14,237 --> 00:07:15,113
Uh…

134
00:07:15,697 --> 00:07:16,656
What?

135
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,493
[Junta] It's just that beetle
really messed up your hair.

136
00:07:20,577 --> 00:07:22,620
What? My hair?

137
00:07:24,664 --> 00:07:25,748
You want me to fix it?

138
00:07:26,541 --> 00:07:27,417
Um…

139
00:07:28,543 --> 00:07:29,419
Could you?

140
00:07:32,130 --> 00:07:34,382
[Junta] You know,
I remember in elementary school,

141
00:07:34,466 --> 00:07:36,843
the kids used to call you
"Frizzy" and "Annie"

142
00:07:36,926 --> 00:07:39,012
because your hair was so red and curly.

143
00:07:39,596 --> 00:07:41,931
[Anzu] They implanted
that memory, too. Devil!

144
00:07:42,599 --> 00:07:43,725
I remember.

145
00:07:44,309 --> 00:07:45,935
Ryuya and his friends used to call me that

146
00:07:46,019 --> 00:07:47,979
because I constantly beat them at games.

147
00:07:49,731 --> 00:07:52,901
Hey, what was that one video game
you used to play all the time?

148
00:07:52,984 --> 00:07:54,319
Cat Ranger?

149
00:07:54,402 --> 00:07:57,655
Yes! Cat Ranger! Oh, that was classic.

150
00:07:57,739 --> 00:08:00,867
It was such an obscure game,
but it was so much fun to play.

151
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:03,870
[Junta] So, what sort of games
are you playing now?

152
00:08:04,454 --> 00:08:07,749
Well, recently, they were all confiscated.

153
00:08:07,832 --> 00:08:09,375
Huh? But what happened?

154
00:08:09,459 --> 00:08:11,753
[Anzu] I keep asking myself
the same thing!

155
00:08:12,837 --> 00:08:14,464
How is it going back there?

156
00:08:14,547 --> 00:08:17,467
Uh, sorry, guess I'm not
so good with my hands.

157
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:18,760
[Anzu] Not good with his hands?

158
00:08:18,843 --> 00:08:20,136
-[Saki] Anzu!
-[both] Huh!

159
00:08:20,887 --> 00:08:21,971
Good morning.

160
00:08:22,055 --> 00:08:23,723
Hey! Morning, Saki.

161
00:08:23,806 --> 00:08:25,517
Hi, Junta. How are you?

162
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,643
Morning.

163
00:08:26,726 --> 00:08:28,603
-[Anzu] Saki knows Junta?
-[giggles]

164
00:08:28,686 --> 00:08:31,481
That little devil got to her, too!

165
00:08:32,649 --> 00:08:35,401
Anzu, do you want me
to help you with your hair?

166
00:08:35,485 --> 00:08:36,611
You wouldn't mind?

167
00:08:36,694 --> 00:08:38,029
That would be great.

168
00:08:38,112 --> 00:08:39,322
[birds chirping]

169
00:08:40,907 --> 00:08:42,534
[Saki] There. Perfect.

170
00:08:42,617 --> 00:08:44,160
You're the best.

171
00:08:44,244 --> 00:08:47,747
You know what? You should start
wearing scrunchies. You look so cute.

172
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:48,957
[laughs]

173
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,333
Junta, your thoughts?

174
00:08:50,416 --> 00:08:51,251
Me?

175
00:08:51,334 --> 00:08:52,252
[exhales]

176
00:08:53,086 --> 00:08:54,003
Yeah.

177
00:08:55,213 --> 00:08:58,132
[Anzu shrieks]
What's with that face?

178
00:08:59,008 --> 00:09:00,176
Oh, thanks.

179
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:03,137
-She totally asked him on purpose.
-[giggles]

180
00:09:05,306 --> 00:09:09,644
Well, Junta's actually a really nice guy.
I wasn't sure what to expect

181
00:09:09,727 --> 00:09:13,439
from my mysterious childhood friend
showing up out of the blue,

182
00:09:13,523 --> 00:09:15,650
but it's kinda weird how comfortable it is

183
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:18,653
-just hanging out with him and Saki.
-She screams so loud.

184
00:09:18,736 --> 00:09:20,822
[Anzu] It almost feels like
we really are old friends.

185
00:09:20,905 --> 00:09:22,156
[laughter]

186
00:09:27,745 --> 00:09:29,205
-[Makoto] Tsukasa.
-Hm?

187
00:09:29,747 --> 00:09:32,667
Morning. Happy to see
you're heading back to school today.

188
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:34,419
Whoa, did you get a new phone?

189
00:09:35,128 --> 00:09:37,589
[Tsukasa] Yeah, can't do anything
without one, so…

190
00:09:38,298 --> 00:09:39,799
-[Rena] Tsukasa!
-Huh?

191
00:09:41,175 --> 00:09:44,596
I can't believe
you just abandoned us like that yesterday.

192
00:09:45,221 --> 00:09:47,807
And to make it worse,
you totally ditched us

193
00:09:47,890 --> 00:09:50,351
-for a girl from another class.
-[sighs]

194
00:09:50,435 --> 00:09:52,979
Wait! Were you really with a girl?

195
00:09:53,062 --> 00:09:54,564
That's different.

196
00:09:54,647 --> 00:09:56,232
Trust me. She's just a friend.

197
00:09:56,816 --> 00:09:58,818
[gasps]
You got a new phone?

198
00:09:59,319 --> 00:10:01,529
Here, let's exchange our numbers.

199
00:10:02,572 --> 00:10:04,240
-I think I'll pass.
-What--

200
00:10:04,324 --> 00:10:07,368
And find someone else to follow around.

201
00:10:09,329 --> 00:10:11,664
No way! Meanie.

202
00:10:12,248 --> 00:10:14,626
Would it kill you to be a little nicer?

203
00:10:14,709 --> 00:10:16,711
If I'm not plunged, she won't learn.

204
00:10:16,794 --> 00:10:18,504
Oh, let me get your number.

205
00:10:19,088 --> 00:10:21,299
-[Makoto] You're really gonna call?
-[Tsukasa sighs]

206
00:10:21,966 --> 00:10:23,259
[groans angrily]

207
00:10:23,885 --> 00:10:25,637
[school bell dings]

208
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:30,308
[Makoto] Whose bright idea was it
to put PE before lunch? I'm starving!

209
00:10:30,892 --> 00:10:33,436
Same. Looking forward
to a home-cooked lunch.

210
00:10:33,519 --> 00:10:35,813
-You always cook for yourself?
-Yeah.

211
00:10:36,481 --> 00:10:38,358
[Makoto] Well,
since you're already making food,

212
00:10:38,441 --> 00:10:40,568
how about you make a little extra for me?

213
00:10:40,652 --> 00:10:42,779
-[Tsukasa] No.
-[Makoto] Doesn't hurt to ask.

214
00:10:43,363 --> 00:10:45,365
[Tsukasa] I'm already making two lunches.

215
00:10:45,865 --> 00:10:47,408
There's a quiz in Math.

216
00:10:47,492 --> 00:10:48,326
[gasps]

217
00:10:49,577 --> 00:10:50,411
Hello.

218
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:51,996
[Tsukasa] Hm.

219
00:10:53,498 --> 00:10:55,917
Hold up. Do you really know Junta Hayami?

220
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,918
Do you know him?

221
00:10:57,502 --> 00:11:00,296
Only the star rookie
of our baseball team this year.

222
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,674
There are rumors that he'll even go pro.

223
00:11:03,299 --> 00:11:06,803
[Tsukasa] I didn't realize Hoshino
had such a popular childhood friend.

224
00:11:07,387 --> 00:11:09,389
How could you not have heard of him?

225
00:11:09,472 --> 00:11:13,059
He's out on the field practicing
almost every free period there is.

226
00:11:13,684 --> 00:11:15,603
Plus, he's tall and good-looking, too.

227
00:11:16,604 --> 00:11:18,940
Don't be jealous.
You're just as good-looking.

228
00:11:20,566 --> 00:11:22,819
-I am not jealous of that guy.
-[scoffs]

229
00:11:22,902 --> 00:11:24,821
-Did you stand us up? Hey.
-Man!

230
00:11:24,904 --> 00:11:26,864
He's gonna be crashing here
at my place for now.

231
00:11:26,948 --> 00:11:29,283
He's… crashing here?

232
00:11:29,867 --> 00:11:32,203
You said you don't wanna date
anyone right now, right?

233
00:11:32,286 --> 00:11:34,205
Oh, great! 'Cause me, too.

234
00:11:37,959 --> 00:11:39,168
Yeah, we'll see.

235
00:11:42,046 --> 00:11:47,135
So, hey, what do you guys know
about that guy? His name is Kazuki.

236
00:11:47,218 --> 00:11:48,302
Oh, I thought you knew him.

237
00:11:48,386 --> 00:11:50,471
No, I just met him this morning.

238
00:11:51,055 --> 00:11:53,057
I've heard of him.
I think he's in Class 7.

239
00:11:53,141 --> 00:11:55,601
I always hear the girls
whispering about him.

240
00:11:55,685 --> 00:11:57,603
So he's pretty popular then.

241
00:11:57,687 --> 00:11:59,480
What? Does that make him your enemy?

242
00:12:00,064 --> 00:12:04,569
He's popular and smart.
He's placed top ten in the midterms.

243
00:12:04,652 --> 00:12:05,486
[Junta] Top ten?

244
00:12:06,195 --> 00:12:08,072
[friend 1] That guy's
on a whole different level.

245
00:12:08,156 --> 00:12:09,365
-[friends] Agreed.
-[sighs]

246
00:12:09,907 --> 00:12:11,993
[team manager] What's with this
slow march down the hall?

247
00:12:12,076 --> 00:12:13,161
Mind if we join?

248
00:12:13,703 --> 00:12:15,663
Oh, hey, guys, look who it is.

249
00:12:15,746 --> 00:12:16,581
Hm.

250
00:12:17,874 --> 00:12:20,209
Do either of you know Tsukasa Kazuki?

251
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:24,297
Kazuki? You mean
the really hot from Class 7?

252
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:26,174
Did you know he's friends with Junta?

253
00:12:26,257 --> 00:12:27,258
Jealous!

254
00:12:27,341 --> 00:12:29,010
Well, more like a friend of a friend.

255
00:12:29,719 --> 00:12:33,431
Uh, question. If he asked to,
I don't know, sleepover at your place,

256
00:12:33,514 --> 00:12:34,515
would you guys let him?

257
00:12:34,599 --> 00:12:37,518
-Oh, my gosh. Yes, of course, I would.
-Mm-hm.

258
00:12:38,102 --> 00:12:41,022
[team manager] Then we fall in love
and live happily ever after.

259
00:12:41,606 --> 00:12:42,648
I figured.

260
00:12:42,732 --> 00:12:44,734
[friend 2] What's up?
You're just as popular as him.

261
00:12:44,817 --> 00:12:46,027
-Hell yeah.
-Hell yeah.

262
00:12:46,110 --> 00:12:50,448
Don't deny it, we all saw you flirting
with that cute girl you grew up with.

263
00:12:50,531 --> 00:12:51,908
You even walked her to school.

264
00:12:53,117 --> 00:12:57,622
Flirt? No, Anzu's just an old friend.
That's all it is, though…

265
00:12:57,705 --> 00:12:59,207
[friends] "Though"? Though what?

266
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:01,542
-I mean… Never mind.
-[friends grunting]

267
00:13:03,044 --> 00:13:05,379
[Junta] They're right, though.
Anzu is really cute.

268
00:13:05,463 --> 00:13:07,131
Her hair, her smile…

269
00:13:07,632 --> 00:13:09,926
No, I can't be thinking this stuff!

270
00:13:10,009 --> 00:13:12,762
Hey, uh, is that really helping anything?

271
00:13:12,845 --> 00:13:14,680
[birds chirping]

272
00:13:18,351 --> 00:13:19,894
I'm sorry, Anzu.

273
00:13:20,394 --> 00:13:22,688
I've got a broadcast club meeting
during lunch today.

274
00:13:23,356 --> 00:13:25,775
Yeah, um-hm, it's all good.

275
00:13:26,943 --> 00:13:28,069
-Bye!
-[Anzu chuckles softly]

276
00:13:28,152 --> 00:13:30,655
[classmate] It's really him,
the hottest boy in Class 7.

277
00:13:31,948 --> 00:13:32,782
Hoshino.

278
00:13:33,407 --> 00:13:34,242
[Anzu] Hm?

279
00:13:35,284 --> 00:13:36,244
Come here.

280
00:13:37,411 --> 00:13:38,246
What?

281
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:43,084
[Saki] Wait. Are those two friends now?
I am so curious.

282
00:13:43,167 --> 00:13:45,378
Ugh, but I'm gonna be late.

283
00:13:48,881 --> 00:13:51,217
[grunts]
You mixed up our lunches.

284
00:13:51,801 --> 00:13:54,720
Yeah, sorry.
I'm not really a morning person.

285
00:13:56,222 --> 00:13:57,974
-[Makoto] Hey, what's up?
-[Tsukasa] Hm?

286
00:13:58,057 --> 00:13:59,392
Tsukasa.

287
00:14:00,059 --> 00:14:01,852
Wait, is that…

288
00:14:03,854 --> 00:14:04,814
Hmm.

289
00:14:04,897 --> 00:14:05,731
Lunches?

290
00:14:06,399 --> 00:14:10,611
She helped me out yesterday
when my place flooded. That's all it is.

291
00:14:11,445 --> 00:14:12,697
Whatever you say.

292
00:14:12,780 --> 00:14:14,198
[Anzu] It's not untrue.

293
00:14:14,282 --> 00:14:15,116
DOESN'T SUSPECT A THING

294
00:14:15,199 --> 00:14:17,493
-Keep this quiet.
-[laughs]

295
00:14:17,577 --> 00:14:20,121
I got you.
Don't want your fans overreacting.

296
00:14:21,205 --> 00:14:22,707
And you are?

297
00:14:22,790 --> 00:14:24,709
I'm Anzu Hoshino.

298
00:14:24,792 --> 00:14:26,335
How's Hosshi sound?

299
00:14:26,419 --> 00:14:27,587
I'm Makoto.

300
00:14:28,713 --> 00:14:31,966
So this must be the girl
Rena was talking about, huh?

301
00:14:32,049 --> 00:14:33,509
What? Not me.

302
00:14:33,593 --> 00:14:35,970
[Makoto] She said
Tsukasa ditched her for you.

303
00:14:36,053 --> 00:14:37,555
[Anzu] Oh, right.

304
00:14:38,598 --> 00:14:39,557
Well, let's go.

305
00:14:42,184 --> 00:14:44,395
This is the perfect place for lunch.

306
00:14:44,478 --> 00:14:45,521
Right, Hosshi?

307
00:14:45,605 --> 00:14:47,899
Oh, okay. Makoto's great.

308
00:14:47,982 --> 00:14:50,026
-He's this nice with everyone?
-Yup.

309
00:14:50,943 --> 00:14:54,113
In case it comes up,
I told them I was staying with family.

310
00:14:54,196 --> 00:14:55,031
[Anzu] Got it.

311
00:14:55,114 --> 00:14:57,658
[light music]

312
00:14:57,742 --> 00:15:01,913
[Makoto] Not fair! That looks delicious.
He refused to make me lunch.

313
00:15:01,996 --> 00:15:03,039
[Tsukasa] Just returning a favor.

314
00:15:03,122 --> 00:15:06,208
Kazuki is a great cook.
He's way better than I am.

315
00:15:06,292 --> 00:15:08,044
That bar's set pretty low.

316
00:15:08,753 --> 00:15:13,215
How about you come over and teach
my mom and sisters how to cook?

317
00:15:13,299 --> 00:15:15,551
Oh, you have a lot of sisters?

318
00:15:16,469 --> 00:15:19,055
Wandering the house in robes, hair a mess…

319
00:15:19,138 --> 00:15:21,515
It's completely jaded to me
when it comes to girls.

320
00:15:21,599 --> 00:15:22,850
[laughs]

321
00:15:22,934 --> 00:15:25,728
Got to say I'm a little jealous.
I'm an only child.

322
00:15:26,312 --> 00:15:28,105
You've got a sister. You know what I mean.

323
00:15:28,189 --> 00:15:30,733
Oh, I didn't know that.
You've never even mentioned her.

324
00:15:31,317 --> 00:15:33,069
[Makoto] Hey, let's see a picture of her.

325
00:15:33,736 --> 00:15:35,071
I don't have one.

326
00:15:36,948 --> 00:15:40,660
Hm. Makoto, is that all
you're eating for lunch?

327
00:15:40,743 --> 00:15:41,744
Heck, yeah.

328
00:15:41,827 --> 00:15:43,245
[gasps]

329
00:15:43,329 --> 00:15:44,664
Chocolate!

330
00:15:44,747 --> 00:15:45,581
CHOCOLATE CORNET

331
00:15:46,165 --> 00:15:48,084
[Makoto] You want some?
I'll split it with you.

332
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:50,586
-Really?
-Way to be cool.

333
00:15:51,212 --> 00:15:52,755
[Makoto] Here, take as much as you want.

334
00:15:52,838 --> 00:15:54,715
-[Anzu] Uh, thanks…
-[Riri] Denied!

335
00:15:54,799 --> 00:15:57,468
[screams, cries]

336
00:15:57,551 --> 00:15:58,594
You okay?

337
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:01,973
Fine. Just remembered, I'm on a diet.

338
00:16:02,056 --> 00:16:04,183
[Anzu] I can't believe I just said that.

339
00:16:04,266 --> 00:16:05,267
A diet? Since when?

340
00:16:05,351 --> 00:16:07,728
I get it. Nothing to be ashamed of.

341
00:16:11,315 --> 00:16:12,316
Hm?

342
00:16:13,025 --> 00:16:14,735
Rena, check it out.

343
00:16:14,819 --> 00:16:16,404
-No joke…
-[Makoto] Yeah.

344
00:16:16,487 --> 00:16:17,822
…you should have seen his face.

345
00:16:17,905 --> 00:16:19,281
-Hilarious!
-[Makoto laughs]

346
00:16:20,324 --> 00:16:22,243
[school bell dings]

347
00:16:22,326 --> 00:16:24,245
[indistinct chatter]

348
00:16:24,829 --> 00:16:26,497
[Anzu] Time to head home.

349
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:30,835
And be bored out of my mind
without any of my games to play.

350
00:16:30,918 --> 00:16:33,587
Guess I could start
looking for a part-time job.

351
00:16:33,671 --> 00:16:35,256
-[Rena] Hoshino.
-Hm?

352
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,966
Got a minute?

353
00:16:38,968 --> 00:16:39,927
Sure?

354
00:16:42,388 --> 00:16:45,558
I'm looking forward to
an afternoon without practice.

355
00:16:45,641 --> 00:16:46,976
Wanna hit the arcade?

356
00:16:47,059 --> 00:16:50,813
Wait, you probably wanna catch up
with your girlfriend, don't ya?

357
00:16:50,896 --> 00:16:53,858
-I told you she's just a friend.
-Yeah, whatever.

358
00:16:53,941 --> 00:16:57,570
Call it what you want, but we know
you want to hang out with her. Go on!

359
00:16:59,196 --> 00:17:00,239
Thanks.

360
00:17:02,324 --> 00:17:03,159
Hey!

361
00:17:04,326 --> 00:17:05,745
[both chuckle]

362
00:17:05,828 --> 00:17:07,955
-You're right.
-Hm, oh…

363
00:17:08,914 --> 00:17:09,749
Junta?

364
00:17:10,416 --> 00:17:13,252
If you're looking for Anzu,
I think she went home already.

365
00:17:13,335 --> 00:17:15,796
Oh, really? She must have missed my text.

366
00:17:16,297 --> 00:17:17,965
You can try calling her.

367
00:17:18,049 --> 00:17:20,551
I've got to run out
to a meeting now. Sorry.

368
00:17:20,634 --> 00:17:22,261
Cool. Have fun.

369
00:17:22,845 --> 00:17:25,097
-Anzu is such a lucky girl.
-Um-hm.

370
00:17:25,181 --> 00:17:27,266
Surrounded by hotties.

371
00:17:29,602 --> 00:17:30,770
[both gasp]

372
00:17:31,395 --> 00:17:32,521
-Hm.
-Hm.

373
00:17:34,899 --> 00:17:38,194
Hey, hang on. Have you seen Anzu?

374
00:17:38,861 --> 00:17:41,197
I can't seem to get a hold of her.

375
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,364
No, I haven't.

376
00:17:43,365 --> 00:17:45,534
Okay, sorry to bother you.

377
00:17:47,244 --> 00:17:48,829
-[Tsukasa gasps]
-[Junta] Huh?

378
00:17:51,165 --> 00:17:54,335
Hm, I found her. This way.

379
00:17:58,672 --> 00:18:01,092
So, uh, you wanted to talk?

380
00:18:01,675 --> 00:18:03,594
I don't think we should be here.

381
00:18:03,677 --> 00:18:06,597
-It looks like a private conversation.
-Hm.

382
00:18:07,431 --> 00:18:08,724
Tell me something.

383
00:18:08,808 --> 00:18:11,227
Do you have a thing for Tsukasa?

384
00:18:11,310 --> 00:18:14,230
What?
[gasping]

385
00:18:14,313 --> 00:18:16,857
Not at all. We're just good friends.

386
00:18:16,941 --> 00:18:18,400
Oh, really?

387
00:18:18,484 --> 00:18:21,445
You say that but you totes have a crush.

388
00:18:21,946 --> 00:18:23,739
No, that's not true.

389
00:18:23,823 --> 00:18:25,533
Do you expect us to believe

390
00:18:25,616 --> 00:18:28,661
you could be just friends with him
when he's that hot?

391
00:18:29,328 --> 00:18:32,206
Of course I do. Believe me.

392
00:18:33,332 --> 00:18:37,753
I am not interested.
I have no interest in dating Tsukasa.

393
00:18:37,837 --> 00:18:39,296
Or anyone else, either.

394
00:18:39,839 --> 00:18:42,091
So you've got nothing to worry about.

395
00:18:42,883 --> 00:18:45,094
My desires are set on
much more important places.

396
00:18:45,177 --> 00:18:46,011
LIFE

397
00:18:47,096 --> 00:18:51,517
What if I was going after him?
It's a free country, you know.

398
00:18:52,101 --> 00:18:53,519
-You're right.
-Mm-hm.

399
00:18:53,602 --> 00:18:54,895
[Anzu] That was easy.

400
00:18:55,855 --> 00:18:56,856
[Rena] So…

401
00:18:57,857 --> 00:19:00,901
Will you help me get his attention
since he's your friend?

402
00:19:01,485 --> 00:19:02,903
You need help?

403
00:19:02,987 --> 00:19:04,238
Duh!

404
00:19:04,321 --> 00:19:07,950
No matter how many times
I ask him out, Tsukasa always says no.

405
00:19:09,118 --> 00:19:12,121
We thought you could set them up.
What do you say?

406
00:19:12,204 --> 00:19:13,831
-[Anzu] Uh…
-You're the best.

407
00:19:15,249 --> 00:19:17,418
-Here. Take my number, okay?
-[phone tapping]

408
00:19:18,002 --> 00:19:19,253
[Rena] Talk soon.

409
00:19:19,879 --> 00:19:20,754
[sighs]

410
00:19:21,505 --> 00:19:24,216
[Rena] Be sure to ask him his type, okay?

411
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:25,176
[gasps]

412
00:19:26,343 --> 00:19:28,971
I'm so over it, seriously.

413
00:19:29,054 --> 00:19:30,806
I'm not interested in dating.

414
00:19:31,390 --> 00:19:32,808
[exhales deeply]

415
00:19:33,517 --> 00:19:35,311
Sorry, can't.

416
00:19:35,394 --> 00:19:36,312
[both gasp]

417
00:19:37,021 --> 00:19:37,897
Huh?

418
00:19:39,899 --> 00:19:40,983
[Rena] Excuse me?

419
00:19:41,066 --> 00:19:44,570
Kazuki told me
he's not looking to date right now.

420
00:19:46,071 --> 00:19:49,408
Out of respect for my friend,
I can't help.

421
00:19:51,327 --> 00:19:52,369
[exhales]

422
00:19:52,953 --> 00:19:54,872
[Junta] She's so cool.

423
00:19:55,623 --> 00:19:57,374
What? Seriously?

424
00:19:57,958 --> 00:19:59,376
[Anzu] Crap. Is she mad?

425
00:20:00,336 --> 00:20:02,880
-[girl] Anzu!
-[sighs, gasps]

426
00:20:02,963 --> 00:20:05,049
Hey, there you are!

427
00:20:05,132 --> 00:20:07,426
I've been looking everywhere for you.

428
00:20:08,469 --> 00:20:09,386
Huh?

429
00:20:09,470 --> 00:20:12,389
[Anzu] Who's she?
Oh, come on. Not another one.

430
00:20:12,473 --> 00:20:14,308
-Are you ready to go home?
-Uh…

431
00:20:14,391 --> 00:20:16,310
Oh, yeah, were you able to find Junta?

432
00:20:16,393 --> 00:20:18,145
He's been looking all over for you.

433
00:20:18,646 --> 00:20:19,897
[growls]

434
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:23,817
[Anzu] What's going on? Is she supposed
to be another long-lost friend?

435
00:20:25,110 --> 00:20:28,405
Anzu, you never told me
you were hanging out with these two girls.

436
00:20:28,989 --> 00:20:31,325
They're only the cutest girls in Class 7!

437
00:20:31,408 --> 00:20:32,409
[both] Huh?

438
00:20:32,493 --> 00:20:35,079
-Cute! Long lashes!
-Oh…

439
00:20:35,162 --> 00:20:39,500
That pixie nose, and your hair…
You are just so pretty!

440
00:20:39,583 --> 00:20:40,918
T-- Thank you!

441
00:20:41,001 --> 00:20:43,754
Wow, such a great figure!

442
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,923
You've gotta tell me

443
00:20:46,006 --> 00:20:48,968
the secret for making
your boobs look so thick.

444
00:20:49,051 --> 00:20:51,804
-Wha--
-It's not easy to make little boobs

445
00:20:51,887 --> 00:20:54,723
push up so high and natural like that.
How do you do it?

446
00:20:54,807 --> 00:20:55,933
-I'm super impressed!
-Hey…

447
00:20:56,517 --> 00:20:59,687
[girl] You can tell me. I get it.
I'm self-conscious about mine, too.

448
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:02,106
But with yours, you worked magic,

449
00:21:02,189 --> 00:21:05,192
they look like a full C cup,
not like Anzu's at all.

450
00:21:05,276 --> 00:21:08,195
[Anzu] What? Is she saying
I can make mine look like that, too?

451
00:21:08,279 --> 00:21:11,240
[girl] I'm so jealous
of your push-up C cup size!

452
00:21:11,323 --> 00:21:12,199
-So huge!
-C cup?

453
00:21:12,283 --> 00:21:13,867
Lovin'!

454
00:21:13,951 --> 00:21:15,494
So perky!

455
00:21:15,577 --> 00:21:17,705
That's enough already, give it a rest!

456
00:21:18,414 --> 00:21:21,417
But I don't think Kazuki
is the kind of guy who'd fall for that,

457
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:23,711
so you really don't have to work so hard.

458
00:21:23,794 --> 00:21:25,212
[groans]

459
00:21:25,796 --> 00:21:28,924
You are rude!
And you're wrong about everything.

460
00:21:29,008 --> 00:21:30,467
Let's go, Yukka.

461
00:21:30,551 --> 00:21:31,719
Coming.

462
00:21:31,802 --> 00:21:34,596
[Yukika] Yeah,
I knew they couldn't be real.

463
00:21:36,015 --> 00:21:38,100
Another job well done! Mm-hm!

464
00:21:38,183 --> 00:21:41,103
[gasps]
Wait a second.

465
00:21:41,687 --> 00:21:44,106
Your cutesy little baby voice.

466
00:21:44,690 --> 00:21:47,651
Your ultra annoying blunt way of speaking.

467
00:21:48,193 --> 00:21:51,071
That oddly familiar star
hanging on your bag.

468
00:21:51,155 --> 00:21:53,782
-[Riri] Kirarin!
-[Anzu] It's you!

469
00:21:55,367 --> 00:21:57,953
-The devil!
-You're wrong.

470
00:21:58,037 --> 00:21:59,621
No devil. Riri.

471
00:21:59,705 --> 00:22:02,249
[Anzu] You're a girl now!

472
00:22:02,333 --> 00:22:05,085
-[giggles]
-[Anzu groans]

473
00:22:06,670 --> 00:22:08,255
A fanfare, please!

474
00:22:08,339 --> 00:22:10,382
And a big congratulations!

475
00:22:10,466 --> 00:22:12,509
Did you fall for my little trick?

476
00:22:12,593 --> 00:22:15,971
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

477
00:22:16,055 --> 00:22:19,558
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

478
00:22:19,641 --> 00:22:22,311
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

479
00:22:22,394 --> 00:22:24,688
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

480
00:22:24,772 --> 00:22:27,357
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

481
00:22:27,441 --> 00:22:29,359
So I can make sure I get paid.

482
00:22:29,443 --> 00:22:31,612
[closing theme music]

483
00:22:31,695 --> 00:22:32,529
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

484
00:22:35,157 --> 00:22:35,991
♪ Let's go! ♪

485
00:22:38,535 --> 00:22:39,661
♪ Lo-love! ♪

486
00:22:41,747 --> 00:22:42,581
♪ Here we go! ♪

487
